From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:30:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] OPP: of: leave CPUs without an OPP table out of a shared one

dev_pm_opp_of_get_sharing_cpus() walks every possible CPU to find the
ones that point at the same opp-shared table, and fails with -ENOENT as
soon as one of them has no OPP table at all. cpufreq-dt reads -ENOENT as
"this CPU has no operating-points-v2" and falls back to a single policy
covering every CPU.

On a system where only some clusters have OPP tables that merges
unrelated clusters into one policy. On the MT6797 Gemini PDA, CPU0-3 and
CPU4-7 each have an opp-shared table and the two Cortex-A72 cores have
none; policy0 came up with related_cpus 0-9 and CPU4-7 got no policy of
their own.

A CPU without an OPP table cannot share this one, so skip it. -ENOENT
still means that the CPU being asked about has no OPP table.
---
 drivers/opp/of.c | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/opp/of.c b/drivers/opp/of.c
index f96adfd5b..5abf98948 100644
--- a/drivers/opp/of.c
+++ b/drivers/opp/of.c
@@ -1305,12 +1305,7 @@ int dev_pm_opp_of_get_sharing_cpus(struct device *cpu_dev,
 		struct device_node *tmp_np __free(device_node) =
 			_opp_of_get_opp_desc_node(cpu_np, 0);
 
-		if (!tmp_np) {
-			pr_err("%pOF: Couldn't find opp node\n", cpu_np);
-			return -ENOENT;
-		}
-
-		/* CPUs are sharing opp node */
+		/* A CPU without an OPP node shares none; leave it out. */
 		if (np == tmp_np)
 			cpumask_set_cpu(cpu, cpumask);
 	}
